config MINIMED_STUB_VOICE
    def_bool y
    depends on MINIMED_SAKE && !SERVICE_VOICE && !SERVICE_VOICE_ENDPOINT
    help
      Link stand-ins for the voice service and the voice endpoint, so a MiniMed build can leave
      voice dictation (and its speex codec) out. Upstream assumes voice is always built: the
      applib dictation window, the process manager, normal-mode service init and the protocol
      endpoint table call into it unconditionally. Dictation then fails like it does without a
      microphone. On by itself whenever a MiniMed build sets CONFIG_SERVICE_VOICE_ENDPOINT=n
      (which also turns SERVICE_VOICE off), since that build cannot link without it. For asterix,
      whose 992 KB flash region cannot hold v4.41.0 and the pump link otherwise.
